<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN AGAIN LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN AGAIN LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse fell to 5.279 billion litas last week from 5.418 billion</p>
<p>litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					     May 26-30     May 19-23</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   17,137	  20,563</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    1,157	   1,999</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)		1,003	   1,255</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	3,271,720     3,454,120</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		  77		372</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    16,770,300    13,520,330</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	60,963,522    58,674,300</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	9,336,514     29,076,760</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    2,339,880     3,425,520</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	    16,770,300    9,694,440</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	    10		7</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	  931,840	 3,854,490</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
